menu "Moto GPS"

config MOTO_TLOG_DISABLE
    bool "Turn off the tlog telemetry recorder (release builds)"
    default n
    help
        The tlog recorder is a development tool: raw IMU samples, attitude,
        acquisition stats and phone GNSS fixes go to the `tlog` flash
        partition for `moto_replay`. Release builds set this (see
        sdkconfig.release): the partition table stays the same, but nothing
        reads, writes or erases the partition, and the sensor task loses its
        4 KiB page writes.

        Phrased as "disable" on purpose: a build directory configured before
        this option existed has no macro at all, and that must mean the
        recorder stays on.

config MOTO_BENCH_TOOLS_DISABLE
    bool "Leave out the bench debug tools (release builds)"
    default n
    help
        The serial console's bench commands (`imu ...`, `sys tasks`,
        `ui page|theme|battery|bench|dbg|perf`, `burnin`, `wifi up|down|forget`,
        `ota confirm`, `tlog clear`), the boot heap probes, the display
        frame-time window that logs every 5 s, and the shared UI's `ui dbg`
        per-layer timers. Release builds set this (see sdkconfig.release): the
        console keeps only `ota status`, `tlog status` and `wifi status`.
        `ota confirm` in particular marks an image valid without the phone's
        handshake, which defeats the rollback guard.

        Phrased as "disable" on purpose, like MOTO_TLOG_DISABLE: a build
        directory configured before this option existed keeps its tools.

endmenu
